      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-95304",
      ":question/problem": "Let $p$ represent the probability that a $6$-sided die lands on $1$. Given the null hypothesis $H_{0}: p = \\frac{1}{6}$, which of the following are valid **two-tailed** alternative hypotheses?\n\n1. $H_{1}: p < \\frac{1}{6}$\n2. $H_{1}: p > \\frac{1}{6}$\n3. $H_{1}: p \\ne \\frac{1}{6}$"
    },
