      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-96463",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\u03bb$ represent the average rate of typos per page in a magazine. Given the null hypothesis $H_{0}: \u03bb = 6$, which of the following are valid two-tailed alternative hypotheses?\n\n1. $H_{1}: \u03bb > 6$\n2. $H_{1}: \u03bb = 6$\n3. $H_{1}: \u03bb \\ne 6$"
